  "hindi": "होता, चेतन पिता, पितरों की सहायता के लिए उत्पन्न हुआ है। यज्ञ करते हुए हम उत्तम धन को, पुरस्कार जीतने वालों के संयम को, सँभालने में समर्थ हों।",
  "english": "The Hotṛ priest, the attentive one, the father, has been born for the help of the fathers. Sacrificing, may we be able to hold the noble good, the restraint of the prize-winners.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The second line is very unclear. prayakṣañ is taken as a present participle 'sacrificing' (it may be a different form of √yaj); jenya as 'noble'; vājinaḥ as genitive plural 'of the prize-winners'; yamam as the noun 'restraint'. The construction of śakema with the accusatives is a guess.",
