  "hindi": "या उसने दौड़ लगाई है, या जब उसने उसके पीछे ब्रह्म कहे; वह पक्षी का ही है। जैसे नेमि चक्र को, वैसे वह सब ज्ञानों को घेरने वाला हुआ।",
  "english": "Either he has run, or when he spoke the prayers after him, that is indeed the bird's. He was around all the wisdoms, like a felly the wheel.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Very unclear verse. dadhanve (taken as perfect of √dhanv 'run') and veru (read as veḥ u 'of the bird, indeed') are tentative; the whole first line may be construed otherwise. brahmāṇi is rendered 'prayers'. In the second line the comparison nemiś cakram iva is taken literally: as the felly surrounds the wheel, he surrounds all wisdoms.",
